 ## [2026-09-25T13:16:54.301Z]
 The manifest-declared package path is normalised to its repository-relative POSIX form once, before any check uses it, so no subject or message can carry a native separator or a trailing slash.
+## [2026-09-26T02:52:38.024Z]
+The pre-publish check told authors a package was ready while the install then refused it: it never compared the version in the package manifest with the marketplace entry, never held requires.yg against the running release, never walked the tree for the symbolic links and binary files the install refuses, and exempted node_modules where the install did not. It now asks everything the install refuses through the very readers the install uses, and leaves out what git ignores because an install clones the tag and never sees it, so a package it passes is one that installs.
+## [2026-09-26T03:36:06.127Z]
+The check left git-ignored files out whenever the marketplace sat anywhere inside a git working tree, but an install reads a source as a repository only at its root; a marketplace nested inside another repository is copied from disk, ignored files and all. The check could therefore pass a package whose ignored node_modules carried a binary that the install then refused. It now asks the install's own question, whether the root is a repository root, before leaving anything out.
